The memory catalog stays where it was first sent

The auto-memory catalog was request-only: every request appended it to the
newest user message and history never kept it. Each new turn therefore
differed from the previous request right before the previous turn's end (the
catalog had moved), and a provider prompt cache had to re-read the previous
question and answer. The main session now attaches the catalog to the
outgoing user or cron message only when the history does not already carry
the current one (first turn, after a memory change, after compression drops
it), so it stays in history where it was sent, is recorded with the sent
content (patch 0007) and replays on resume. appendAutoMemoryContext adds
its request-only copy only when the history's newest catalog is outdated, so
subagents, side queries and tool-result requests keep seeing the current
catalog.

